# `lib/` is SOURCE here, not build output: this package ships plain JavaScript with no build step,
# which is how it keeps "clone and install" free of a toolchain. It was ignored while the package was
# still a reservation; leaving that line in would have meant committing a plugin whose entry point
# does not exist in the repository.

# *.tgz is `npm pack` output. It is the artifact whose sha1 the release check compares against the
# registry, so it has to stay reproducible rather than committed -- and three stale tarballs showing up
# in `git status` is how a release commit ends up carrying a binary nobody reviewed.
